    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11505" root="خمس" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَاؤُوا خُمَاسَ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْمَسَ</span></b> , <i>They came five
and five;</i> [or <i>five and five together; or five at a
time and five at a time;</i>] (K, TA;) like as they
say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُنَآءَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَثْنَى</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَاعَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْبَعَ</span>: (TA:)
or, accord. to A 'Obeyd, not more than <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُحَادَ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُنَآءَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُلَاثَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَاعَ</span> has been heard, except
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُشَارَ</span> occurring in a verse of El-Kumeyt. (TA in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عشر</span>.)

